65
00:03:04,170 --> 00:03:07,290
kidneys, they're located
below the diaphragm, and

66
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:10,350
they're retroperitoneal. So
what does that mean? They're

67
00:03:10,350 --> 00:03:13,570
outside the peritoneum. so
they're basically attached

68
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:17,490
to the body cavity wall on
the back of the abdominal

69
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:21,650
cavity unlike the GI
organs which are mostly

70
00:03:21,650 --> 00:03:26,790
within the peritoneum and
free-floating kidneys are

71
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:30,670
towards the back and basically
span the length of t12

72
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:34,290
to l3 with the right kidney
being lower than the left

73
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:38,310
because of the liver each
kidney there's two right

74
00:03:38,310 --> 00:03:42,150
are being shaped with the
medial side called the hilum

75
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:45,810
containing blood vessels
and the ureters exiting.

76
00:03:46,490 --> 00:03:50,150
They're both covered by a
dense elastic connective

77
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:52,650
tissue sheath called
the renal fascia.

78
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:55,590
It envelopes not only
the kidney but also the

79
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:58,830
suprarenal glands or
the adrenal glands. The

80
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:01,850
kidneys are deceptively
small which is kind of

81
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:04,530
a testament to how much
they do for the body.

82
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:08,050
The kidneys only take
up about 0.5 percent

83
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:11,010
of total body weight.
But despite this,

84
00:04:11,010 --> 00:04:12,950
the blood flow through
them is massive.

85
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:15,850
I know you guys haven't
had cardio yet, but

86
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:19,170
cardiac output is heart
rate times stroke volume.

87
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:22,870
So the normal cardiac output

88
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:24,990
per minute is
about five liters.

89
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:29,230
The kidneys receive 20%
of this each minute, so

90
00:04:29,230 --> 00:04:32,270
about one liter, which
once again is fascinating

91
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:35,310
considering how small
the organs are. You can

92
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:39,230
basically fit 150 cc's
of fluid in each kidney

93
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:43,130
so that would mean over
three times the amount

94
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:45,750
of that fluid flows
through them each minute.

95
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:49,010
You can see on the left
of this slide the entire

96
00:04:49,010 --> 00:04:52,510
